/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(>> Solution to Question 1:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Detail the three hierarchical levels of Biodiversity \(Genetic, Species, and Ecosystem Diversity\) and explain their evolutionary foundations.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Hierarchical Structure and Evolutionary Mechanics of Biodiversity:) Tj
T*
(   1. Genetic Diversity:) Tj
T*
(   - Definition: The total variety of genetic information contained in all the individual) Tj
T*
(   organisms of a species, encompassing allelic variation within populations and chromosomal) Tj
T*
(   differences between geographically separated populations.) Tj
T*
(   - Molecular Foundations: Generated by point mutations, meiotic crossing-over, independent) Tj
T*
(   assortment, and chromosomal rearrangements.) Tj
T*
(   - Evolutionary Function: High genetic heterozygosity provides the raw material for natural) Tj
T*
(   selection. Populations with high allelic richness possess the plasticity required to adapt to) Tj
T*
(   novel environmental stresses \(pathogen outbreaks, thermal shifts, droughts\). Genetic uniformity) Tj
T*
(   \(monoculture\) increases susceptibility to catastrophic extinction.) Tj
T*
(   2. Species Diversity:) Tj
T*
(   - Definition: The variety, richness, and relative abundance of distinct biological species) Tj
T*
(   coexisting within a defined ecological community.) Tj
T*
(   - Structural Dimensions: Combines Species Richness \(the simple tally of unique species present\)) Tj
T*
(   and Species Evenness \(the equitability of individual abundances across those species\).) Tj
T*
(   - Functional Significance: High species diversity stabilizes ecosystem productivity via) Tj
T*
(   functional redundancy: if one pollinator or decomposer declines, other species with overlapping) Tj
T*
(   ecological niches sustain ecosystem processes.) Tj
T*
(   3. Ecosystem \(Landscape\) Diversity:) Tj
T*
(   - Definition: The diversity of physical habitats, ecological communities, and biogeochemical) Tj
T*
(   processes across a broad landscape or bioregion.) Tj
T*
(   - Encompasses variations in trophic complexity, structural vertical stratification, and) Tj
T*
(   microclimatic gradients across terrestrial, aquatic, and transitional ecotone biomes.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
