(   [Problem Statement]: Analyze the Rodgers and Panwar Biogeographic Classification of India, describing the characteristics of its 10 Biogeographic Zones.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Rodgers and Panwar Biogeographic Classification of India:) Tj
T*
(   1. Scientific Basis of Classification:) Tj
T*
(   Formulated in 1988 by W.A. Rodgers and H.S. Panwar \(Wildlife Institute of India\), this) Tj
T*
(   framework categorizes India's geographic territory into 10 distinct Biogeographic Zones based) Tj
T*
(   on macroclimate, topography, floristic affinity, and zoogeographical distribution:) Tj
T*
(   2. The 10 Biogeographic Zones:) Tj
T*
(   - 1. Trans-Himalaya \(5.6% of land area\): Cold arid high-altitude desert plateaus \(Ladakh,) Tj
T*
(   Lahaul-Spiti\). Flora: sparse dwarf alpine steppe \(Caragana, Artemisia\). Fauna: Snow Leopard,) Tj
T*
(   Tibetan Wild Ass \(Kiang\), Ibex, Black-necked Crane.) Tj
T*
(   - 2. Himalaya \(6.4%\): Subtropical foot-slopes to alpine tundra across Northwest, West, Central,) Tj
T*
(   and East Himalayas. High floristic endemism \(Rhododendrons, conifers\). Fauna: Musk Deer,) Tj
T*
(   Himalayan Tahr, Monal Pheasant.) Tj
T*
(   - 3. Desert \(6.6%\): Arid Thar Desert of Rajasthan and Rann of Kutch. Highly specialized) Tj
T*
(   xerophytes \(Prosopis cineraria, Capparis\). Fauna: Great Indian Bustard, Indian Wild Ass \(Khur\),) Tj
T*
(   Desert Fox.) Tj
T*
(   - 4. Semi-Arid \(16.6%\): Transition zone between desert and peninsula \(Gujarat, dry parts of) Tj
T*
(   Punjab, Haryana, Rajasthan\). Dry deciduous and thorn forests \(Acacia, Anogeissus\). Fauna:) Tj
T*
(   Asiatic Lion \(Gir\), Blackbuck, Chinkara.) Tj
T*
