(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   India as a Mega-Diversity Nation: Biogeographical and Taxonomic Synthesis:) Tj
T*
(   1. Global Standing and Land Area Disparity:) Tj
T*
(   India is officially recognized by UNEP and Conservation International as one of the world's 17) Tj
T*
(   Mega-diverse nations. Occupying merely 2.4% of the global terrestrial surface area, India) Tj
T*
(   harbors approximately 7% to 8% of all recorded global species!) Tj
T*
(   2. Floristic and Faunal Wealth:) Tj
T*
(   - Flora: Over 49,000 documented plant species \(~11% of global flora\), including over 18,000) Tj
T*
(   flowering angiosperms, with nearly 33% of vascular flora strictly endemic to India.) Tj
T*
(   - Fauna: Over 102,000 recorded animal species \(~6.7% of global fauna\):) Tj
T*
(   * Mammals: 428 species \(~8.6% of global total, including large iconic mammals: Asian Elephant,) Tj
T*
(   Bengal Tiger, Asiatic Lion, Snow Leopard, One-horned Rhino\).) Tj
T*
(   * Birds: 1,350+ species \(representing ~13% of global avian diversity\).) Tj
T*
(   * Reptiles & Amphibians: Over 500 reptile and 400 amphibian species \(Western Ghats has over 80%) Tj
T*
(   amphibian endemism\).) Tj
T*
(   3. Primary Vavilov Center of Crop Origin:) Tj
T*
(   India is one of the world's 12 original Vavilov centers of plant genetic diversity, possessing) Tj
T*
(   over 160 species of cultivated food crops and over 320 wild relatives of crops \(rice,) Tj
T*
(   sugarcane, pigeonpea, mango, citrus, turmeric, black pepper, cardamom\). This gene pool is vital) Tj
T*
(   for cross-breeding disease resistance into modern crops.) Tj
T*
(   4. Marine and Coastal Wealth:) Tj
T*
(   A continuous coastline exceeding 7,500 km, an Exclusive Economic Zone \(EEZ\) of 2.02 million) Tj
T*
(   km2, rich coral reef complexes \(Gulf of Mannar, Andaman & Nicobar, Lakshadweep\), and extensive) Tj
T*
(   mangrove deltas \(Sundarbans, the world's largest contiguous mangrove ecosystem\).) Tj
T*
