12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Analyze the anthropogenic drivers of Biodiversity loss using E.O. Wilson's HIPPO framework, illustrating each with empirical evidence.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   The HIPPO Framework of Biodiversity Loss: Mechanisms and Empirical Case Studies:) Tj
T*
(   Formulated by Edward O. Wilson, HIPPO identifies five synergistic anthropogenic pressures) Tj
T*
(   driving the modern Sixth Mass Extinction:) Tj
T*
(   1. H - Habitat Loss, Fragmentation, and Degradation:) Tj
T*
(   - Primary driver worldwide. Conversion of primary forests, wetlands, and grasslands into urban) Tj
T*
(   infrastructure, highways, open-pit mines, and monoculture croplands.) Tj
T*
(   - Habitat Fragmentation: Bisecting continuous forest tracts by roads isolates wildlife) Tj
T*
(   populations into small habitat islands, creates extensive desiccating edge effects, and) Tj
T*
(   restricts migratory gene flow, inducing inbreeding depression.) Tj
T*
(   2. I - Invasive Alien Species:) Tj
T*
(   - Introduction of non-native organisms that outcompete native species due to the absence of) Tj
T*
(   co-evolved predators and diseases:) Tj
T*
(   - Terrestrial: Lantana camara and Parthenium hysterophorus suppress native understory) Tj
T*
(   regeneration.) Tj
T*
(   - Aquatic: Water hyacinth \(Eichhornia crassipes\) forms thick surface mats blocking light and) Tj
T*
(   suffocating benthic aquatic life.) Tj
T*
(   3. P - Pollution:) Tj
T*
(   - Industrial effluents, organochlorine pesticides \(biomagnifying up food chains\), synthetic) Tj
T*
(   fertilizer runoff driving aquatic eutrophication, heavy metal toxicity, plastic micro-particles) Tj
T*
(   in marine food webs, and acid precipitation.) Tj
T*
(   4. P - Population Growth \(Human\):) Tj
T*
(   - Exponential growth of human population \(surpassing 8 billion\) escalates per capita) Tj
T*
(   consumption of natural resources, driving deforestation, water abstraction, and conversion of) Tj
T*
(   wildlife habitats.) Tj
T*
(   5. O - Overexploitation and Poaching:) Tj
T*
(   - Unsustainable hunting, commercial poaching, and illegal wildlife trade:) Tj
T*
(   - Rhinoceros poached for keratin horn, Tigers for bones and skins, Elephants for ivory tusks,) Tj
T*
(   Pangolins for keratin scales \(the world's most trafficked mammal\), and oceanic industrial) Tj
T*
(   bottom trawling causing collapse of commercial fisheries.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
