(   1. Evolutionary Hypotheses of Invasiveness:) Tj
T*
(   - Enemy Release Hypothesis \(ERH\): In their introduced range, exotic invasive plants escape the) Tj
T*
(   specialist insect herbivores, foliar nematodes, and fungal pathogens that regulated their) Tj
T*
(   population densities in their native co-evolved range.) Tj
T*
(   - Novel Weapons Hypothesis: Invasive plants synthesize and exude unique allelopathic secondary) Tj
T*
(   metabolites \(phytotoxins\) into the rhizosphere that native soil microbes and competing plant) Tj
T*
(   roots have never encountered, inhibiting native seed germination.) Tj
T*
(   - Rapid Phenotypic Plasticity & High Reproductive Output: Enormous seed production, efficient) Tj
T*
(   bird/wind dispersal, broad physiological tolerance across diverse soil pH and moisture) Tj
T*
(   conditions.) Tj
T*
(   2. Case Study: Lantana camara:) Tj
T*
(   - Origin and Spread: Native to tropical South America, introduced as an ornamental hedge in) Tj
T*
(   India in 1807. Now blankets over 13 million hectares of Indian forest land.) Tj
T*
(   - Ecological Impact:) Tj
T*
(   * Dense, impenetrable thorny thickets shade out tree seedlings, arresting natural forest) Tj
T*
(   succession.) Tj
T*
(   * Foliage contains toxic triterpenoids \(Lantadene A and B\), causing severe hepatotoxicity,) Tj
T*
(   photosensitization, and death in grazing livestock.) Tj
T*
(   * Birds consume the drupe fruits, dispersing seeds over vast distances.) Tj
T*
(   3. Case Study: Parthenium hysterophorus \(Congress Grass / Carrot Grass\):) Tj
T*
(   - Introduced accidentally into India in the 1950s as a grain contaminant in wheat consignments) Tj
T*
(   under the US PL-480 program.) Tj
T*
(   - Allelopathy & Human Pathology:) Tj
T*
(   * Roots and trichomes secrete sesquiterpene lactones \(primarily Parthenin\) and caffeic acid,) Tj
T*
(   inhibiting germination and root elongation of native grasses and agricultural crops.) Tj
T*
(   * Foliar trichomes and airborne pollen cause severe allergic contact dermatitis, eczema,) Tj
T*
(   rhinitis, and respiratory asthma in rural human populations.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
