BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(>> Solution to Question 8:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Detail the IUCN Red List Categories, the quantitative criteria for 'Critically Endangered' \(CR\), and the status of threatened Indian wildlife.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   IUCN Red List Categories, Quantitative Extinction Risk Criteria, and Indian Threatened Fauna:) Tj
T*
(   1. Structural Architecture of IUCN Categories \(Version 3.1\):) Tj
T*
(   - Evaluated:) Tj
T*
(   * Extinct \(EX\): No reasonable doubt that the last individual has died.) Tj
T*
(   * Extinct in the Wild \(EW\): Survives only in captivity or cultivation.) Tj
T*
(   * Threatened Categories:) Tj
T*
(   - Critically Endangered \(CR\): Facing an extremely high risk of extinction in the wild.) Tj
T*
(   - Endangered \(EN\): Facing a very high risk of extinction in the wild.) Tj
T*
(   - Vulnerable \(VU\): Facing a high risk of extinction in the wild.) Tj
T*
(   * Near Threatened \(NT\): Close to qualifying for a threatened category.) Tj
T*
(   * Least Concern \(LC\): Widespread and abundant.) Tj
T*
(   * Data Deficient \(DD\): Inadequate information to make an assessment.) Tj
T*
(   2. Quantitative Criteria for 'Critically Endangered' \(CR\):) Tj
T*
(   A taxon qualifies as Critically Endangered if it meets ANY ONE of the following quantitative) Tj
T*
(   thresholds:) Tj
T*
(   - Criterion A \(Population Reduction\): Observed, estimated, or inferred reduction of >= 90% over) Tj
T*
(   10 years or 3 generations where causes are reversible AND understood, OR >= 80% where causes) Tj
T*
(   may NOT be reversible.) Tj
T*
(   - Criterion B \(Geographic Range\): Extent of Occurrence \(EOO\) estimated at < 100 km2, OR Area of) Tj
T*
(   Occupancy \(AOO\) < 10 km2, accompanied by severe fragmentation or continuing decline.) Tj
T*
(   - Criterion C \(Small Population Size\): Mature breeding population estimated at < 250 mature) Tj
T*
