(   [Problem Statement]: Analyze the legal and spatial provisions for Protected Areas under the Wildlife \(Protection\) Act, 1972: National Parks vs. Wildlife Sanctuaries.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Statutory Architecture of Protected Areas under the Indian Wildlife \(Protection\) Act, 1972:) Tj
T*
(   1. National Parks \(Section 35\):) Tj
T*
(   - Declaration: Declared by State Governments \(or Central Government\) over areas of significant) Tj
T*
(   ecological, faunal, floral, geomorphological, or zoological importance for the purpose of) Tj
T*
(   protecting, propagating, or developing wildlife.) Tj
T*
(   - Strict Legal Protection:) Tj
T*
(   * Zero Human Habitation: Private land rights inside a National Park must be fully acquired and) Tj
T*
(   extinguished \(settlement of rights under Land Acquisition Act\).) Tj
T*
(   * Prohibition of Resource Exploitation: Complete ban on forestry exploitation, timber) Tj
T*
(   harvesting, non-timber forest produce \(NTFP\) collection, and livestock grazing.) Tj
T*
(   * No alteration of boundaries permitted except upon recommendation of the National Board for) Tj
T*
(   Wildlife \(NBWL\).) Tj
T*
(   2. Wildlife Sanctuaries \(Section 26A\):) Tj
T*
(   - Declaration: Declared over areas of adequate ecological, faunal, or floral significance.) Tj
T*
(   - Legal Framework:) Tj
T*
(   * Regulated Human Activities: Private ownership rights inside a Sanctuary can be permitted to) Tj
T*
(   continue by the District Collector.) Tj
T*
(   * Grazing and Traditional Rights: The Chief Wildlife Warden may authorize limited, regulated) Tj
T*
(   livestock grazing, transit, and traditional fishing if deemed non-detrimental to wildlife) Tj
T*
(   conservation.) Tj
T*
(   3. Conservation Reserves and Community Reserves \(Sections 36A and 36C\):) Tj
T*
(   - Introduced by the 2002 Amendment to incorporate participatory community conservation:) Tj
T*
(   * Conservation Reserves: Government-owned lands adjacent to National Parks acting as ecological) Tj
T*
(   corridors, managed by a committee comprising local village representatives.) Tj
T*
(   * Community Reserves: Private or community-owned lands where local communities volunteer to) Tj
T*
(   conserve wildlife.) Tj
T*
