(   [Problem Statement]: Examine the ecological and sociocultural role of Sacred Groves in India as micro-refugia for endangered botanical and faunal germplasm.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Sacred Groves of India: Ethnobotanical Significance and Ecological Micro-Refugia:) Tj
T*
(   1. Anthropological and Cultural Origins:) Tj
T*
(   Sacred groves are patches of near-climax natural forest conserved by local indigenous rural and) Tj
T*
(   tribal communities through ancestral religious beliefs, cultural taboos, and traditional) Tj
T*
(   customary laws. Dedicated to local deities or ancestral spirits \(e.g., Ayyanar in Tamil Nadu,) Tj
T*
(   Vaghdev in Maharashtra\), all commercial tree felling, hunting, and destructive grazing are) Tj
T*
(   strictly prohibited by societal taboos.) Tj
T*
(   2. Regional Nomenclature and Distribution:) Tj
T*
(   - Maharashtra: Devrai / Devrahat.) Tj
T*
(   - Rajasthan: Orans / Kenkris \(associated with Bishnoi villages\).) Tj
T*
(   - Kerala: Kavu \(Sarpa Kavu dedicated to serpent deities\).) Tj
T*
(   - Meghalaya: Law Kyntang / Law Lyngdoh \(conserved by Khasi and Jaintia tribes\).) Tj
T*
(   - Himachal Pradesh: Deovans.) Tj
T*
(   3. Ecological and Biogeochemical Functions:) Tj
T*
(   - Micro-Refugia for Threatened Germplasm: Many sacred groves represent the last surviving) Tj
T*
(   relict fragments of the region's original primary climax vegetation that has otherwise been) Tj
T*
(   cleared for agriculture. They harbor critically endangered, rare, and threatened \(RET\)) Tj
T*
(   medicinal plants, wild orchids, and lianas.) Tj
T*
(   - Hydrological Micro-Catchments: Dense forest canopy and thick leaf litter act as natural) Tj
T*
(   sponge catchments, recharging local groundwater aquifers, perennial freshwater springs, and) Tj
T*
(   village community wells.) Tj
T*
(   - Nutrient Reserves & Soil Protection: Prevent severe soil erosion on steep hillslopes and) Tj
T*
(   preserve ancient mycorrhizal fungal networks and soil invertebrate diversity.) Tj
T*
