(   [Problem Statement]: Detail the conservation strategy of Project Tiger \(1973\), including core-buffer metapopulation management and M-STrIPES digital monitoring.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Project Tiger: Institutional Architecture, Core-Corridor Metapopulation Model, and Technology:) Tj
T*
(   1. Historical Genesis and Mandate \(1973\):) Tj
T*
(   Following the historic 1972 nationwide tiger census revealing that wild Bengal Tiger \(Panthera) Tj
T*
(   tigris tigris\) populations had collapsed from ~40,000 in 1900 to under 1,827 due to colonial) Tj
T*
(   trophy hunting and habitat loss, the Government of India launched Project Tiger on April 1,) Tj
T*
(   1973, in Jim Corbett National Park.) Tj
T*
(   2. Core-Buffer-Corridor Metapopulation Management:) Tj
T*
(   The National Tiger Conservation Authority \(NTCA, statutory body under Wildlife Protection Act\)) Tj
T*
(   administers over 54 designated Tiger Reserves:) Tj
T*
(   - Inviolate Core / Critical Tiger Habitat \(CTH\): Legally protected under Section 38V, core) Tj
T*
(   areas must be maintained inviolate from all human disturbance. Voluntary relocation of) Tj
T*
