(   [Problem Statement]: Analyze the objectives of Project Elephant \(1992\), elephant corridor fragmentation, and mitigation of Human-Elephant Conflict \(HEC\).) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Project Elephant, Elephant Corridors, and Mitigation of Human-Elephant Conflict:) Tj
T*
(   1. Project Elephant Mandate \(1992\):) Tj
T*
(   Launched by the Ministry of Environment and Forests, Project Elephant provides financial and) Tj
T*
(   technical support to major elephant-bearing states with three primary objectives:) Tj
T*
(   - Protecting Asian Elephants \(Elephas maximus\), their habitats, and migratory corridors.) Tj
T*
(   - Addressing and mitigating human-elephant conflict \(HEC\).) Tj
T*
(   - Ensuring the veterinary welfare of captive domesticated elephants.) Tj
T*
(   2. The Critical Role of Elephant Corridors:) Tj
T*
(   - Elephants are mega-herbivores requiring vast home ranges \(200 to 1,000 km2\) and consuming 150) Tj
T*
(   to 200 kg of forage daily. They undertake seasonal trans-landscape migrations following water) Tj
T*
(   sources and forage phenology.) Tj
T*
(   - Linear Infrastructure Fragmentation: Railway tracks bisecting corridors cause frequent lethal) Tj
T*
(   train collisions \(e.g., in Assam and northern West Bengal\). Highways, irrigation canals, and) Tj
T*
(   high-voltage transmission lines fragment traditional migratory routes.) Tj
T*
(   3. Human-Elephant Conflict \(HEC\) Mechanics:) Tj
T*
(   When migratory corridors are severed, elephant herds divert into human agricultural croplands) Tj
T*
(   \(paddy, sugarcane, banana\), causing severe crop depredation, property damage, and loss of human) Tj
T*
(   and elephant lives.) Tj
T*
(   4. Engineering and Biological Mitigation Interventions:) Tj
T*
(   - Underpasses & Canopy Bridges: Constructing dedicated wildlife underpasses beneath elevated) Tj
T*
(   highway and railway corridors.) Tj
T*
(   - Early Warning Systems: AI-driven thermal imaging cameras and acoustic fiber-optic sensors) Tj
T*
(   along railway tracks alerting locomotive drivers to elephant herd movements.) Tj
T*
(   - Deterrent Barriers: Installing hanging solar-powered electric fencing, deep elephant-proof) Tj
T*
(   trenches \(EPTs\), and biological chili-smoke fences or beehive fencing \(elephants naturally) Tj
T*
(   avoid stinging bees\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
