(   processes:) Tj
T*
(   - Immigration \(Colonization\) of new species from the mainland source pool \(P\).) Tj
T*
(   - Extinction of established resident species on the island.) Tj
T*
(   2. Mathematical Formulations:) Tj
T*
(   - Colonization Rate Curve I\(S\):) Tj
T*
(   * When an island is barren \(S = 0\), colonization is at its maximum \(I_0\). As the island fills) Tj
T*
(   with resident species, the probability that an incoming colonist belongs to a novel) Tj
T*
(   unrepresented species declines monotonically to zero when S = P:) Tj
T*
(   I\(S\) = I_0 * \(1 - S / P\)) Tj
T*
(   * Island Isolation Effect: Islands situated closer to the mainland exhibit steeper, higher) Tj
T*
(   colonization curves than distant, isolated islands.) Tj
T*
(   - Extinction Rate Curve E\(S\):) Tj
T*
(   * When S = 0, extinction is zero. As species accumulate, interspecific competition for finite) Tj
T*
(   island space and food intensifies, and average population size per species declines, increasing) Tj
T*
(   the risk of stochastic demographic extinction:) Tj
T*
(   E\(S\) = E_max * \(S / P\)) Tj
T*
(   * Island Area Effect: Large islands possess larger carrying capacities and greater habitat) Tj
T*
(   heterogeneity, supporting larger population sizes that exhibit lower extinction rates than) Tj
T*
(   small islands.) Tj
T*
(   3. Equilibrium Equations and Species Turnover:) Tj
T*
(   - Dynamic Equilibrium Species Richness \(S*\):) Tj
T*
(   Set I\(S\) = E\(S\):) Tj
T*
(   I_0 * \(1 - S* / P\) = E_max * \(S* / P\)) Tj
T*
(   I_0 - I_0 * \(S* / P\) = E_max * \(S* / P\)) Tj
T*
(   I_0 = \(I_0 + E_max\) * \(S* / P\)) Tj
T*
(   => S* = P * [ I_0 / \(I_0 + E_max\) ]) Tj
T*
(   - Equilibrium Species Turnover Rate \(T*\):) Tj
T*
(   At equilibrium S*, species composition is NOT static; new species continually arrive while) Tj
T*
(   existing species disappear:) Tj
T*
(   T* = I\(S*\) = E\(S*\) = \(I_0 * E_max\) / \(I_0 + E_max\)) Tj
T*
(   - Application to Habitat Reserves: Nature reserves function as ecological islands surrounded by) Tj
T*
(   hostile agricultural/urban matrices \(the SLOSS debate: Single Large or Several Small reserves\).) Tj
T*
