(   allow unrestricted animal dispersal and gene flow.) Tj
T*
(   - Isolated Oceanic Islands / Habitat Fragments: z rises to 0.25 to 0.35 due to dispersal) Tj
T*
(   barriers and elevated extinction risks.) Tj
T*
(   3. Predicting Extinctions from Habitat Fragmentation:) Tj
T*
(   - If an original contiguous habitat of area A_0 harboring S_0 species is reduced to a) Tj
T*
(   fragmented area A_new:) Tj
T*
(   S_new / S_0 = \(A_new / A_0\)^z) Tj
T*
(   - Fractional Species Loss \(Delta S / S_0\):) Tj
T*
(   Loss = 1 - \(S_new / S_0\) = 1 - \(A_new / A_0\)^z) Tj
T*
(   - Quantitative Case Study:) Tj
T*
(   If 90% of a tropical rainforest is deforested \(A_new / A_0 = 0.10\) and island fragmentation) Tj
T*
(   exponent z = 0.30:) Tj
T*
(   S_new / S_0 = \(0.10\)^0.30 approx 0.501.) Tj
T*
(   Conclusion: A 90% reduction in continuous habitat area leads over time to an irreversible 50%) Tj
T*
(   loss of total biological species through extinction debt.) Tj
