(   [Problem Statement]: Detail the Nagoya Protocol on Access and Benefit Sharing \(ABS\), explaining Prior Informed Consent \(PIC\) and Mutually Agreed Terms \(MAT\).) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   The Nagoya Protocol on Access and Benefit Sharing \(ABS\): Legal Architecture:) Tj
T*
(   1. International Legal Origin \(2010\):) Tj
T*
(   Adopted at the 10th Conference of the Parties \(COP-10\) to the Convention on Biological) Tj
T*
(   Diversity \(CBD\) in Nagoya, Japan, the Nagoya Protocol provides a transparent legal framework) Tj
T*
(   for the third pillar of the CBD: the fair and equitable sharing of benefits arising from the) Tj
T*
(   utilization of genetic resources and traditional knowledge.) Tj
T*
(   2. Core Operational Mechanisms:) Tj
T*
(   - Sovereign Rights over Biological Resources: Reaffirms that national governments have) Tj
T*
(   sovereign rights over their biological resources within their territorial jurisdiction.) Tj
T*
(   - Prior Informed Consent \(PIC\):) Tj
T*
(   * Users \(foreign pharmaceutical companies, biotechnology researchers\) must obtain explicit,) Tj
T*
(   legally binding permission from the National Competent Authority of the provider country prior) Tj
T*
(   to collecting or accessing genetic resources or indigenous traditional knowledge.) Tj
T*
(   - Mutually Agreed Terms \(MAT\):) Tj
T*
(   * Users and provider countries/indigenous communities must negotiate formal contractual terms) Tj
T*
(   governing conditions of access and the precise nature of benefit-sharing.) Tj
T*
(   3. Benefit-Sharing Typologies:) Tj
T*
(   - Monetary Benefits: Upfront access fees, milestone research payments, and ongoing commercial) Tj
T*
(   royalties derived from patented biotechnology products.) Tj
T*
(   - Non-Monetary Benefits: Scientific technology transfer, collaborative joint research) Tj
T*
(   publications, training of indigenous scientists, and local infrastructure development.) Tj
T*
(   4. Prevention of Biopiracy: Establishes national compliance checkpoints \(customs, patent) Tj
T*
(   offices\) to verify that patent applicants have legitimate PIC and MAT certificates.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(>> Solution to Question 24:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Examine the Cartagena Protocol on Biosafety, detailing the Advance Informed Agreement \(AIA\) procedure for Living Modified Organisms \(LMOs\).) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   The Cartagena Protocol on Biosafety and Regulation of Living Modified Organisms \(LMOs\):) Tj
T*
(   1. Protocol Mandate \(2000\):) Tj
T*
(   Adopted under the CBD to protect biological diversity and human health from potential adverse) Tj
T*
(   risks posed by Living Modified Organisms \(LMOs, modern Genetically Modified Organisms\)) Tj
T*
(   resulting from modern biotechnology that are capable of replication or transferring genetic) Tj
T*
(   material.) Tj
T*
(   2. The Precautionary Principle \(Principle 15 of Rio Declaration\):) Tj
T*
(   The protocol explicitly operationalizes the Precautionary Principle: 'Lack of full scientific) Tj
T*
(   certainty due to insufficient relevant scientific information and knowledge regarding the) Tj
T*
(   extent of the potential adverse effects shall not prevent that Party from taking a decision...) Tj
T*
ET

