(   [Problem Statement]: Analyze the Millennium Ecosystem Assessment classification of Ecosystem Services, and describe Economic Valuation methodologies.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Ecosystem Services Classification and Environmental Economic Valuation:) Tj
T*
(   1. The Four Typologies of Ecosystem Services \(MA, 2005\):) Tj
T*
(   Initiated by the United Nations, the Millennium Ecosystem Assessment categorized ecological) Tj
T*
(   benefits into four functional classes:) Tj
T*
(   - 1. Provisioning Services: Tangible material products extracted directly from ecosystems:) Tj
T*
(   freshwater, timber, edible crops, natural fibers, genetic medicinal resources.) Tj
T*
(   - 2. Regulating Services: Benefits obtained from the natural regulation of ecosystem processes:) Tj
T*
(   climate regulation via carbon sequestration, water purification by wetlands, coastal flood) Tj
T*
(   dissipation by mangroves, agricultural pollination by native bees.) Tj
T*
(   - 3. Cultural Services: Non-material benefits enriching human psychological, spiritual, and) Tj
T*
(   intellectual well-being: religious sacred landscapes, aesthetic hiking recreation, wildlife) Tj
T*
(   ecotourism, educational research.) Tj
T*
(   - 4. Supporting Services: Foundational ecological processes necessary for the production of all) Tj
T*
(   other ecosystem services: pedogenesis \(soil formation\), primary photosynthetic biomass) Tj
T*
(   production, and biogeochemical nutrient cycling.) Tj
T*
(   2. Environmental Economic Valuation Methodologies:) Tj
T*
(   Because ecosystem services are largely public goods lacking market prices, environmental) Tj
T*
(   economists employ non-market valuation tools:) Tj
T*
(   - Hedonic Pricing Method: Estimates environmental values by observing property price) Tj
T*
(   differentials associated with environmental amenities \(e.g., homes bordering clean lakes vs) Tj
T*
(   polluted waters\).) Tj
T*
(   - Travel Cost Method: Quantifies recreational and aesthetic value of national parks by) Tj
T*
(   calculating travel expenditures incurred by visitors.) Tj
T*
(   - Contingent Valuation Method \(CVM\): Survey-based stated preference technique directly asking) Tj
T*
(   individuals their Willingness to Pay \(WTP\) to protect a specific ecosystem service, or) Tj
T*
(   Willingness to Accept \(WTA\) compensation for its loss.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
