(   [Problem Statement]: Analyze the impacts of Climate Change on montane biodiversity, explaining the 'Elevational Escalator Effect' and phenological mismatch.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Climate Change Impacts on Montane Ecosystems: Escalator Effect and Phenological Mismatches:) Tj
T*
(   1. Montane Vulnerability and Adiabatic Lapse Rates:) Tj
T*
(   Mountain ecosystems exhibit steep vertical bioclimatic zonation compressed over short) Tj
T*
(   horizontal distances. Ambient air temperature declines with altitude according to the) Tj
T*
(   environmental adiabatic lapse rate: ~6.5 deg C cooling per 1,000 meters elevation gain.) Tj
T*
(   2. The 'Elevational Escalator Effect':) Tj
T*
(   - As global surface temperatures rise, thermal isotherms shift upward to higher altitudes.) Tj
T*
(   - Montane plant and animal species track their co-evolved thermal niches by shifting their) Tj
T*
(   geographic distributions upslope.) Tj
T*
