(   [Problem Statement]: Detail the legal battles over Indian Biopiracy \(Neem, Turmeric, Basmati\) and evaluate the Traditional Knowledge Digital Library \(TKDL\).) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Biopiracy of Indian Traditional Knowledge and the Defensive Architecture of TKDL:) Tj
T*
(   1. Definition of Biopiracy:) Tj
T*
(   The commercial exploitation and patenting of naturally occurring biochemical compounds or) Tj
T*
(   traditional indigenous knowledge by multinational corporations without obtaining Prior Informed) Tj
T*
(   Consent \(PIC\) or providing equitable benefit sharing to the originating indigenous communities.) Tj
T*
(   2. Classic Landmark Indian Biopiracy Cases:) Tj
T*
(   - 1. The Turmeric \(Curcuma longa\) Patent Battle \(1995\):) Tj
T*
(   * The US Patent and Trademark Office \(USPTO\) granted Patent No. 5,401,504 to the University of) Tj
T*
(   Mississippi for the 'Use of Turmeric in Wound Healing.') Tj
T*
(   * The Council of Scientific and Industrial Research \(CSIR, India\), led by Dr. R.A. Mashelkar,) Tj
T*
(   challenged the patent by submitting 32 ancient Ayurvedic Sanskrit texts and Urdu medical) Tj
T*
(   journals proving that the topical wound-healing property of turmeric was centuries-old public) Tj
T*
(   domain prior art. The USPTO revoked all patent claims in 1997.) Tj
T*
(   - 2. The Neem \(Azadirachta indica\) Fungicidal Patent:) Tj
T*
(   * In 1995, the European Patent Office \(EPO\) granted Patent No. 436257 to the USDA and W.R.) Tj
T*
(   Grace for the fungicidal properties of neem oil extract. Following a 10-year legal challenge by) Tj
T*
(   Indian NGOs and Vandana Shiva proving prior public use in Indian agriculture, the EPO revoked) Tj
T*
(   the patent in 2005.) Tj
T*
(   - 3. The Basmati Rice Patent:) Tj
T*
(   * In 1997, US corporation RiceTec was granted US Patent No. 5,663,484 on 'Basmati rice lines) Tj
T*
(   and grains.' CSIR challenged the patent, forcing RiceTec to withdraw major claims.) Tj
T*
(   3. The Traditional Knowledge Digital Library \(TKDL\):) Tj
T*
(   - Established in 2001 as a collaborative initiative of CSIR and the Ministry of AYUSH.) Tj
T*
(   - Translates public ancient Indian medical knowledge \(Ayurveda, Unani, Siddha, Sowa-Rigpa\) from) Tj
T*
(   classical languages \(Sanskrit, Arabic, Persian, Tamil\) into five international patent languages) Tj
T*
(   \(English, French, German, Japanese, Spanish\) using proprietary Traditional Knowledge Resource) Tj
T*
(   Classification \(TKRC\) codes.) Tj
T*
(   - Integrated into global patent examiner search systems \(EPO, USPTO, JPO\), enabling examiners) Tj
T*
(   to identify prior art instantly, proactively defeating hundreds of biopiracy patent) Tj
T*
(   applications worldwide.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
